1. Init Containers

What is Init Container?

An Init Container is a special container that runs before the main application container starts in a Pod.

👉 It runs only once and must complete successfully before the app container starts.

🎯 Why we use Init Containers?

	Setup environment before app starts

	Wait for dependencies (DB, API, etc.)

	Download configuration/files

	Run migrations or initialization scripts


👉 Flow:

	1. Init container runs

	2. Completes successfully

	3. Then main container starts

Example YAML (Init Container)

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: init-container-demo
spec:
  containers:
  - name: app
    image: nginx
  initContainers:
  - name: init-myservice
    image: busybox
    command: ['sh', '-c', 'echo Initializing... && sleep 10']

How to Test Init Container

1. Create pod

	kubectl apply -f init.yaml

2. Check pod status

	kubectl get pods

3. Describe pod (see init container logs)

	kubectl describe pod init-container-demo

4. Check logs of init container

	kubectl logs init-container-demo -c init-myservice

